  "id": "wisconsin-card-sorting-test",
  "term": "Wisconsin Card Sorting Test",
  "definition": "The Wisconsin Card Sorting Test is a neuropsychological assessment used to evaluate executive function, especially abilities linked with the frontal lobe such as abstract thinking and planning. In it, the person sorts response cards by changing rules and must shift strategy as the task changes.",
